<title>FRANCE: EU to tie GAN aid to '98 sell-off - source.</title>
<headline>EU to tie GAN aid to '98 sell-off - source.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission will approve the French government's 20 billion francs of aid for GAN in exchange for a privatisation of the ailing insurer by June 30, 1998, a source close to the deal said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Commission sources said on Monday that the state aid package would be approved at the Commission's weekly meeting on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The package consists of a capital injection of 11 billion francs and a further nine billion in state guarantees to cover property losses.</p>
<p>GAN's CIC bank network will also have to be sold off, either with GAN or separately, the source said.</p>
<p>A further condition is the disposal of half GAN's network outside France in the 12 months after privatisation.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
